# Class and Student Relationships

Before creating or changing a page:

- Inspect existing models, services, API contracts, and role permissions.
- Reuse the existing Class and Student records; never create parallel catalogs.
- Never ask users to type `className` or `studentName` when selecting an existing entity.
- Load classes from the role-scoped API and bind the selected `classId`.
- After class selection, request only that class roster from the backend.
- Clear `studentId` whenever `classId` changes.
- Save relationship IDs only (`classId`, `studentId`, or `studentIds`).
- Do not send denormalized Class/Student names in create/update requests.
- Resolve names through backend relationships in read responses.
- Include loading, empty, API-error, required-field, and stale-request handling.
- Enforce tenant and role scope server-side; frontend filtering is not authorization.

Manual names are valid only while creating/editing the Class or Student entity
itself, not while referencing it from attendance, fees, homework, exams,
library, certificates, transport, reports, or other modules.

Do not modify the existing enrollment forms or `enrollmentService.js` for this
rule unless the user explicitly requests enrollment changes.
